              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "secō, secāre — \"to cut, to slice\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Pater pānem cultellō secuit. Father sliced the bread with a little knife."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "secō, secāre, secuī, sectum. English section and insect, a creature cut into parts, come from it."
            }
          ]
