          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "secō is inherited from the Proto-Indo-European root sek-, \"to cut\" (EtymDB). English section, sector and insect come from it."
